    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="235a7941-8bc3-5193-8303-f522a708b9a1" activityNameId="90243f56-4df7-54d6-b323-d63073af1d2b" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xxx Round wood, Scandinavian softwood, under bark, u=70% at forest road</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xxx Round wood, Scandinavian softwood, under bark, u=70% at forest road
The volume does not include the bark. CO2 assimilation is based on 49.4% carbon in the wood. Biomass energy equals gross calorific value including bark.;
UUID: 56c23a35-7fd2-3b4c-affb-ce4ebb1220aa
This module includes material and energy amounts for stand establishment, tending, site development, thinnings and final cutting of scandinavian round softwood (logs for sawmill), its transport to the nearest forest road as well as the land and materials use for the forest roads
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Modern average technology used in Scandinavia
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: Allocation to roundwood (logs) and industrial wood already made by authors of the finnish LCA database. Allocation factors unknown.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_56c23a35-7fd2-3b4c-affb-ce4ebb1220aa.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
